        "proposed_action": {
            "actor": "furnace captain Nia Brindle, citing TC 910 C and Kilnveil 420 mm",
            "summary": "reline BOF-2 and change the taphole sleeve; 4 ns TOF is a wet-gun glitch",
            "basis_claimed": "last-campaign Kilnveil and the shell TC are both consistent with 420 mm so the path cannot be 300 mm",
        },
        "safety_decision": {
            "decision": "ACCEPT",
            "rationale": "This vessel is accepted, not the taphole and not BOF-1. Serialized reconstruction: n = sqrt(er) = sqrt(4.00) = 2.00; d_m = c * dt / (2 n) = 3.00e8 * 4.00e-9 / (2 * 2.00) = 0.300; d_mm = 300.0, which is 20 mm under the 320 mm reline floor and 120 mm above the 180 mm isolate floor. SOP rev C still forbids the taphole sleeve: ordered reline of BOF-2 this campaign only. Explicit scope: this accept does not cover taphole changes and does not authorize BOF-1 without a new path frame. Isolate tripwire: d_mm <= 180.",
            "threshold": "d_mm<=320 AND d_mm>180 AND vessel=BOF-2 AND taphole_not_changed",
            "stated_residuals": "20 mm margin is not infinite; 4.00 dielectric still carries moisture; shell TC is not a lining-thickness witness",
        },
        "executed_action": {
